# {{ package_name.capitalize() }} RPM

RPM packaging for [{{ package_name }}]({{ package_url }}).

To create an rpm/srm, simply use the included makefile running:

```bash
make rpm
```

and 

```bash
make srpm
```

respectively.

## Releases

Releases are created automatically when a version bump is merged into `main`. To cut a new release:

1. Update `Version:` (and/or `Release:`) in the spec file under `dist/`.
2. Add a matching `%changelog` entry at the top, for example `* Fri Nov 20 2026 Jane Doe <jdoe@example.com> - 1.1.0-1`.

Once merged, the release workflow tags `<version>-<release>`, creates a GitHub release using that changelog entry as the release notes, and uploads the built RPMs and SRPMs. If the changelog entry for an existing release is edited later, the release notes are updated to match. The workflow fails if the newest changelog entry does not match the spec version.

This repository is based on the [NSLS2 standard RPM packaging template](https://github.com/NSLS2/rpm-repo-template). To update the template to the most recent version, run:

```bash
pixi run update-template
```

Note that you may need to resolve merge conflicts after updating.
